## Anti-Patterns to Avoid

- Never use `any` type unless absolutely necessary
- Avoid inline function definitions in JSX when possible
- Don't use index as a key for mapped arrays
- Avoid deeply nested component structures
- Don't mutate props or state directly
- Avoid premature optimization
- Don't modify shadcn/ui component source code without documentation
- Don't remove focus styles without providing alternatives

```tsx
// ❌ Bad: Using index as key
{
  items.map((item, index) => <ListItem key={index} item={item} />);
}

// ✅ Good: Using unique identifier as key
{
  items.map((item) => <ListItem key={item.id} item={item} />);
}
```

## Accessibility

- Always use semantic HTML elements
- Include alt text for images
- Ensure keyboard navigation works
- Use ARIA attributes when necessary
- Test with screen readers
- Leverage shadcn/ui's accessible components which are built on Radix UI primitives

```tsx
